t APIs yet, so I'll need to add stub implementations.\n\nLet me check what's already available in the internal module and what gaps need filling.\n\nLooking at the test requirements, I see several patterns emerging: `header_length` needs functions like `predict_packet_header_length` and methods on `Quic` for packet creation and retransmission management, while `packet_enc_dec` is much more involved, requiring encryption/decryption stubs and stream data node management on the `Quic` type. Many of these functions don't exist yet in the codebase.\n\nMy approach will be to translate the tests directly to the Rust API as intended, filling in missing methods with `todo!()` stubs. For `parseheader`, I need to stub out packet header parsing, connection ID management functions, path access methods, and header creation utilities. For `packet_enc_dec`, I'll need similar encryption and decryption infrastructure.\n\nThese tests dig into a lot of internal implementation details, so I'll translate them pragmatically, stubbing out the deep internal state manipulation as needed.\n\nThe `packet_enc_dec` test is particularly intricate since it requires direct manipulation of crypto contexts, so I need to be careful with that translation.\n\nLet me check what's already available in the internal and lib modules to see what stubs I can work with.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4912,"cache_read_input_tokens":77660,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4912},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4dc870de-e938-4c75-83bb-2bc85323ae97","uuid":"b4a89597-0a8d-4686-af79-19e168b3361b"}
