{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XNjnENG2ydKWLvxR2V4qEd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Translation of `quic/qlog.h`.\n2\t//!\n3\t//! Header-only module exposing a single entry point that turns\n4\t//! on per-connection qlog tracing for a QUIC context.  The body\n5\t//! lives in `loglib/autoqlog.c` (a separate target, out of scope\n6\t//! for v1); this module is the picoquic-core stub that links\n7\t//! against it on demand.\n8\t\n9\tuse std::path::Path;\n10\t\n11\tuse crate::{Quic, Result};\n12\t\n13\timpl Quic {\n14\t    /// Enable qlog tracing on this context, writing one qlog file per\n15\t    /// connection into `qlog_dir`.  Installs the unified-logging\n16\t    /// vtable; subsequent connections on this context will stream\n17\t    /// qlog records until the context is dropped.\n18\t    ///\n19\t    /// Both observed call sites guard on the directory being set\n20\t    /// before calling, so the parameter is borrowed (no\n21\t    /// `Option<…>`); the C `int` status (0 / -1) becomes\n22\t    /// `Result<()>`.\n23\t    ///\n24\t    /// C: `int set_qlog(Quic*, char const*)`.\n25\t    pub fn set_qlog(&mut self, _qlog_dir: &(impl AsRef<Path> + ?Sized)) -> Result<()> {\n26\t        todo!()\n27\t    }\n28\t}\n29\t\n30\t#[cfg(test)]\n31\tmod test {}\n32\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4dc870de-e938-4c75-83bb-2bc85323ae97","uuid":"83f5813c-3aa9-466d-bf81-11c227ffd9a2","timestamp":"2026-05-05T05:18:57.169Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/qlog.rs","content":"//! Translation of `quic/qlog.h`.\n//!\n//! Header-only module exposing a single entry point that turns\n//! on per-connection qlog tracing for a QUIC context.  The body\n//! lives in `loglib/autoqlog.c` (a separate target, out of scope\n//! for v1); this module is the picoquic-core stub that links\n//! against it on demand.\n\nuse std::path::Path;\n\nuse crate::{Quic, Result};\n\nimpl Quic {\n    /// Enable qlog tracing on this context, writing one qlog file per\n    /// connection into `qlog_dir`.  Installs the unified-logging\n    /// vtable; subsequent connections on this context will stream\n    /// qlog records until the context is dropped.\n    ///\n    /// Both observed call sites guard on the directory being set\n    /// before calling, so the parameter is borrowed (no\n    /// `Option<…>`); the C `int` status (0 / -1) becomes\n    /// `Result<()>`.\n    ///\n    /// C: `int set_qlog(Quic*, char const*)`.\n    pub fn set_qlog(&mut self, _qlog_dir: &(impl AsRef<Path> + ?Sized)) -> Result<()> {\n        todo!()\n    }\n}\n\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod test {}\n","numLines":32,"startLine":1,"totalLines":32}}}
