{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n\nThe user requested a Phase 3A batch translation of 5 C test sources from `picoquictest/` into Rust `#[test]` bodies under `rs/fq/src/tests/`. The batch covers:\n- `parseheadertest` → 4 tests: `parseheader()`, `incoming_initial()`, `header_length()`, `packet_enc_dec()`\n- `picolog_test` → 1 test: `picolog_basic()`\n- `picoquic_lb_test` → 2 tests: `cid_for_lb()`, `cid_for_lb_cli()`\n- `pn2pn64test` → 1 test: `pn2pn64()` (already complete)\n- `qlog_frame_test` → 1 test: `qlog_frames()`\n\nRules:\n- No `todo!()` placeholders in test bodies (translate faithfully)\n- Add `todo!()` stubs for missing API methods in `rs/fq/src/{internal,lib}.rs`\n- No `unsafe`, no edits outside `rs/fq/src/tests/`, `rs/fq/tests/fixtures/`, or stub additions\n- Gate: `cargo fmt && cargo test --no-run && cargo clippy --tests --all-features -- -D warnings`\n- Verify each source with `python3 scripts/phase3_check.py <source_basename>`\n- Golden/fixture files go in `rs/fq/tests/fixtures/`\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n- **C-to-Rust translation**: Test-driven development, tests don't need to pass, just compile cleanly and express the API design\n- **picoquic QUIC library**: Single-threaded, virtual-time, QUIC transport implementation in C\n- **`rs/fq/` crate**: Rust translation target; modules: `lib.rs` (public API), `internal.rs` (internals), `tls_api.rs`, `lb.rs`, `qlog.rs`, `binlog.rs`, `frames.rs`\n- **Packet header types**: `PacketHeader`, `PacketType`, `Epoch`, `PacketContext` in `internal.rs`\n- **Connection/Path model**: `Quic` → `Connection` → `Path` → `Tuple` → local/remote CIDs\n- **Packet contexts**: 3 QUIC packet number spaces; Rust enum values: `PacketContext::Application=0`, `Handshake=1`, `Initial=2` (REVERSED from C's `initial=0, handshake=1, application=2`)\n- **Epochs**: `Epoch::Initial=0`, `ZeroRtt=1`, `Handshake=2`, `OneRtt=3` (matches C)\n- **LB CID**: Load balancer connection ID generation/verification via `crate::lb`\n- **TLS API test helpers**: `setup_test_aead_context`, `pn_enc_create_for_test` in `crate::tls_api`\n- **Borrow conflict resolution**: Many existing stubs take `&mut self` AND `&mut PacketContextState`/`&mut Path` — need path0-specific wrappers to avoid borrow conflicts in tests\n- **`Version::InternalTest1 = 0x50435130`** — used in `create_connection` calls\n- **fugit time types**: `Instant::from_ticks(usec)`, `Duration::from_ticks(usec)`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n- **`xlate/test_translation_guide.md`** (read)\n   - Authoritative reference for Rust API surface, naming conventions, translation patterns\n   - Key: `Quic::new(11 args)`, `Quic::create_connection(9 args)`, `Quic::create_client_connection`, `ConnectionId::clone_from_slice`, `ConnectionId::with_size`\n   - `crate::internal` has `PacketHeader`, `PacketType`, `Epoch`, `parse_16/24/32/64`, `get_packet_number64`, `create_packet_header`, `update_payload_length`\n   - `crate::lb` has `Config`, `ConnectionIdContext`, `Quic::set_lb_cid_config`, `Quic::clear_lb_cid_config`\n\n- **`rs/fq/src/tests/util.rs`** (read, ~1061 lines)\n   - Has `TestTlsApiCtx`, `tls_api_one_scenario_init_ex`, `tls_api_connection_loop`, `cert_verify_set_ctx`, `tls_api_init_ctx_ex`, etc.\n   - Missing: `TestSkipFrameEntry`, `TEST_SKIP_FRAMES` (need to add)\n\n- **`picoquictest/parseheadertest.c`** (read, 1216 lines)\n   - Defines 9 test packet byte arrays and expected `picoquic_packet_header` structs\n   - `parseheadertest()`: parse loop + encode loop over 9 entries\n   - `incoming_initial_test()`: calls `packet_initial_dec_one(packet_intel_bug)` — creates server Quic with certs, calls `picoquic_incoming_packet_ex`\n   - `header_length_test()`: 55 cases, tests `predict_packet_header_length` == `create_packet_header` actual length\n   - `packet_enc_dec_test()`: client/server Quic, initial→handshake→0rtt→1rtt encrypt/decrypt cycle\n\n   Key test data: `TEST_CNXID_INI_BYTES = 0x00,0x01,0x02,0x03,0x04,0x05,0x06,0x07` (len=8), `TEST_CNXID_REM_BYTES = 0x04,0x05,0x06,0x07` (len=4), `TEST_CNXID_LOCAL_BYTES = 0x01..0x08` (len=8), `TEST_CNXID_10_BYTES = 0x02..0x09` (len=8)\n\n- **`picoquictest/picolog_test.c`** (read, 165 lines)\n   - `picolog_basic_test()`: opens binary log + SVG template, builds CID set via `binlog_list_cids`, verifies count>0, prints CID set, checks specific CID not in set, iterates calling `svg_convert`, compares SVG output to reference\n   - Paths: `picoquictest/picolog_test_input.log`, `loglib/template.svg`, `picoquictest/svglog_ref.svg`\n\n- **`picoquictest/picoquic_lb_test.c`** (read in parts, ~1215 lines)\n   - `cid_for_lb_test()`: creates Quic, iterates 58 test cases; each: `set_lb_cid_config`, invoke CID callback (`generate`), verify generated CID matches reference, `verify` to get server ID, `clear_lb_cid_config`\n   - `cid_for_lb_cli_test()`: parses 9 config strings with `Config::parse`, compares fields; tests 9 bad strings expect error; fuzz test substituting characters\n   - 58 test configs with `method`, `rotation_bits`, `first_byte_encodes_length`, `server_id_length`, `nonce_length`, `connection_id_length`, `server_id`, `cid_encryption_key[16]`\n\n- **`picoquictest/pn2pn64test.c`** (read, 89 lines)\n   - Simple: 36 test cases `{highest, mask, pn, expected}`, calls `get_packet_number64(highest, mask, pn)`\n\n- **`picoquictest/qlog_frame_test.c`** (read, 74 lines)\n   - Opens output JSON file, iterates `test_skip_list` (from `skip_frame_test.c`), calls `qlog_frames(F, bytes, bytes_max, 0)` for each entry, compares to `picoquictest/qlog_frames_test_ref.txt`\n\n- **`rs/fq/src/tests/pn2pn64test.rs`** (read) - **Already complete** with all 36 cases using `get_packet_number64`\n\n- **`rs/fq/src/tests/parseheadertest.rs`** (read) - All 4 stubs with `todo!()`\n\n- *